#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kate;"
msgstr "Apontiaedje di &kate;"

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "configure"
msgstr "apontyî"

#. Tag: secondary
#: configuring.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "settings"
msgstr "apontiaedjes"

#. Tag: tertiary
#: configuring.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "preferences"
msgstr "preferinces"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; offers several means of tweaking the application to behave as "
"desired. The most important ones are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Configuration Dialog"
msgstr "Li purnea d'pontiaedje"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main configuration tool, allowing you to configure the &kate; "
"application, the editor component and the usage of plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr "Li menu <guimenu>Apontiaedjes</guimenu>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to change often used settings, and to launch the configuration "
"dialogs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr "Li menu <guimenu>Vey</guimenu>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to split the current frame, as well as to display the icons and "
"line numbers pane for the currently edited document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The embedded &konsole; is using the configuration defined in the "
"&kcontrolcenter;, and may be configured by clicking the "
"<mousebutton>right</mousebutton> mouse button and choosing from the "
"<guimenuitem>Settings</guimenuitem> sub menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Configuration Dialog"
msgstr "Li purnea des mwaissès apontiaedjes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kate; configuration dialog displays a tree of topics on the left, and a "
"configuration page corresponding to the selected topic on the right. The "
"tree groups the pages of the dialog into logical groups."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kate; group"
msgstr "Li groupe &kate;"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "This group contains pages to configure the main &kate; application"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "The General Page"
msgstr "Li pådje djeneråle"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Global Options for &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Application Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>MDI</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>MDI</primary>"

#. Tag: secondary
#: configuring.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>SDI</secondary>"
msgstr "<secondary>SDI</secondary>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group lets you choose between &kate; <acronym>MDI</acronym> and &kate; "
"<acronym>SDI</acronym> mode, selecting the appropriate button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; <acronym>MDI</acronym> (Multiple Document Interface), which is the "
"default mode, makes &kate; use a single window for all open files. You can "
"choose the document to edit from the File List (docked into the &kate; "
"window by default) or by selecting the document from the "
"<guimenu>Document</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; <acronym>SDI</acronym> (Single Document Interface) will make &kate; "
"open each document in a window of its own, and the File List/File Selector "
"will have a separate window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you change this setting, you will need to restart &kate; for it to take "
"effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "At Startup"
msgstr "A l' enondaedje"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These options determine how and if &kate; will restore your editing session "
"when launched after a normal shutdown (if restored by the session manager, "
"&kate; will always attempt to restore your session as close as possible to "
"what it was when you last used &kate;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reopen Files"
msgstr "Ridrovi les fitchîs"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, files open when you last closed &kate; will be "
"reopened. Bookmarks will be restored, and the cursor position, icon border "
"and line numbers settings for the last editor used with the document will be "
"reestablished"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restore View Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, &kate; will attempt to restore your frames "
"exactly as you left them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restrict to single instance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enabling this means you can only have one running instance of &kate; running "
"at any given time. If you attempt to start another one, the current instance "
"will take over and also open files as requested. For example, if you use "
"&kate; for displaying sources for web pages in Konqueror, they will all be "
"opened in an existing instance of &kate; if this option is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Contents While Resizing Frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, the windows will be fully repainted while "
"dragging the frame splitters. If unchecked, a so-called <quote>rubber "
"band</quote> (indicating the new size of the frame) will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sync Konsole with Active Document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will cause the built-in &konsole; to <command>cd</command> into the "
"directory of the active document when launched and when a new document gets "
"the focus. If not enabled, you have to do all your navigation in the "
"&konsole; on your own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of Recent Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unsurprisingly, this allows you to decide how long the <guimenu>Open "
"Recent</guimenu> files menu should grow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Editor Group"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "This group contains all pages related to the editor component of &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> Page"
msgstr "Li pådje des <guilabel>Coleurs</guilabel>"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to change the background and selection background "
"colors of the editor. Initially, &kate; will use the colors as set in the "
"&kcontrolcenter; "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Look'n'Feel</guimenu><guimenuitem>Colors</guimenuitem> "
"</menuchoice> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change a color, press the associated button and select the desired color "
"in the color chooser."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choosing the background color may render Syntax Highlighted text unreadable. "
"You should use a light color for the background, and a dark color for the "
"selection background."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Otherwise, you will probably need to change the <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-highlight-default-styles\">Default "
"Styles</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Fonts Page"
msgstr "Li pådje des fontes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to choose the default fonts for &kate;. The settings "
"will be used for the &kwrite; and for viewing text files in &konqueror; as "
"well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The page presents two tabs, one for the editor font and one for the printing "
"font. Select a tab and choose the desired font. The default is to use the "
"&kde; global setting for fixed font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As it is not currently possible to use individual fonts for documents, nor "
"to change the font for printing from the print dialog, be careful. A "
"fixed-width font is strongly recommended."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Indent Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "This page allows you to change the behavior of indentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indent Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto indent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, &kate; will automatically indent new lines equal to the previous "
"line. If the previous line is blank, the nearest above line with contents is "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indent with Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "If checked, &kate; will indent with spaces rather than tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backspace key indents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, &kate; will unindent equal to the nearest above line "
"with contents when you press the <keycap>Backspace</keycap> key if the part "
"of the line preceding the cursor contains only whitespace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab key indents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, &kate; will indent the current line equal to the nearest "
"above line with content when you press the <keycap>Tab</keycap> key, if the "
"part of the line preceding the cursor contains only whitespace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep extra spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this behavior checked, &kate; will leave whitespace behind the cursor "
"after indenting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Select Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "This page provides options for fine tuning the select behavior of &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persistent Selections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When Persistent Selections is enabled, key input will not cause the "
"selection to be removed/diminished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option partly conflicts with the Overwrite Selection option. If both "
"are enabled, pasting text or pressing any other keys than the arrow keys "
"will cause the selection to be overwritten."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overwrite Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, any text insertion, whether typed or pasted will cause "
"the selected text to be deleted and replaced with the inserted text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Edit Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page contains miscellaneous options for fine-tuning the behavior of the "
"&kate; editor component."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editor Options"
msgstr "Tchuzes di l' aspougneu"

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "Word Wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Word Wrap as used here means dynamically format the text by breaking lines "
"at an appropriate place, rather than soft wrapping lines in the editor for "
"easier reading."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will insert a line break as defined by the <link "
"linkend=\"document-end-of-line\">End of Line</link>"
" setting for the document when the line extends the length set in <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-edit-wrap-words-at\">Wrap Words At</link> "
"option described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wrap Words At"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option decides the max length of lines if the <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-edit-word-wrap\">Word Wrap</link> option is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace Tabs with Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will replace inserted <keycap>Tab</keycap> characters "
"with a number of single whitespace characters as defined in <link "
"linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-edit-tab-indent-width\">Tab Width</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove trailing spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will remove any whitespace at the rear end of a line each "
"time the cursor is moved off that line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab/Indent Width"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the tab width, which is also used to decide the amount of indentation "
"when <link linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-indent-auto-indent\">Auto "
"Indent</link> is enabled, or indentation is otherwise called for."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the <link linkend=\"config-dialog-editor-indent\">Indent</link>"
" settings indentation may be caused by pressing the <keycap>Tab</keycap>"
" and <keycap>Backspace</keycap> keys, and activating the <link "
"linkend=\"edit-indent\"><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Indent</guimenuitem></link> menu entry will call for indent as "
"well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto Brackets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, &kate; will automatically insert a right bracket "
"immediately to the right of the cursor when a left bracket is inserted from "
"the keyboard. The supported bracket types are <keycap>(</keycap>, "
"<keycap>{</keycap>, <keycap>[</keycap>and <keycap>&lt;</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group undos"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will group any number of similar editing actions (for "
"example typing, backspacing, pasting) in one entry in the undo history, so "
"they can all be undone at once."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Tabs"
msgstr "Mostrer les tabulåcions"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kate; will draw a small dot at the start of a "
"<keycap>Tab</keycap> character in the editor to indicate its presence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid "Smart Home"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will make &kate; move the cursor to the first non-whitespace character "
"of the current line rather than to the absolute beginning, when the "
"<keycap>Home</keycap> key (or other key assigned to that function) is "
"pressed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: configuring.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wrap Cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, moving the cursor past the end of a line will cause it to "
"continue to the next/previous line if any."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not enabled, the cursor cannot be moved right of the beginning of the "
"line, but it may be moved past the end of line, and when text is inserted "
"&kate; will automatically insert whitespace up to that position. This is "
"sometimes very handy for programmers, for example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Keyboard Page"
msgstr "Li pådje del taprece"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can configure the keyboard shortcuts for the internal commands of "
"the &kate; editor component. These includes commands for moving around in "
"the document and selecting text. For keys related to copying and pasting "
"text, see The Configure Keys Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "You may change the keys for a command, or add an alternate key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "To change the key(s) for a command, follow this procedure:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the command for which you want to configure the keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the <guibutton>None</guibutton> option in the pane below the list if "
"you don't want a key for this command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the <guibutton>Default</guibutton> option to use the default key(s) "
"for the command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the <guibutton>Custom</guibutton> option to select a custom key for "
"the command, or set an alternate one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose the <guibutton>Custom</guibutton> option, the key entering "
"button at the right of the pane will be enabled. To set a key, press it. The "
"&kde; Define Shortcut Dialog will appear. In this dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose whether to set the default or alternate key. "
"<guilabel>Default</guilabel> does not mean that you change the application "
"default for this action, rather it sets the custom standard key for it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press the desired key sequence, it will be visualized for you in the dialog "
"for your confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are of an adventurous nature, try playing around with the "
"<guibutton>Multikey</guibutton> option. Using it will allow you to have "
"&Emacs;-like key sequences (one key enters a group, the next performs the "
"action), apart from the fact that instead of just doing the job, &kde; will "
"pop up a menu to choose from in an undefined and most likely inappropriate "
"place. You will now be in no doubt as to whether pressing the next key in "
"the sequence will work, or you have to type the menu accelerator (both will "
"work)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Spelling Page"
msgstr "Li pådje del coridjrece"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "This page allows you to configure how &kspell; behaves with &kate;"
msgstr "Cisse pådje ci c' est po-z apontyî li dujhance di &kspell; avou &kate;"

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Highlighting Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to fine tune the color and syntax type selection of "
"&kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid "For more in depth information on the syntax highlighting system, see ??"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The page consists of two tabs, one for setting the <guibutton>Default "
"styles</guibutton> and one for managing the <guibutton>Highlight "
"Modes</guibutton>"
". Both tabs display a list of contexts in which the default colors and font "
"are used to visualize the look of each style. The context name is painted "
"using the current properties of the context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "The list has four or five columns, each with the following purpose:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:570
#, no-c-format
msgid "Context"
msgstr "Contecse"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays the context name, painted using the style properties for the "
"context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bold"
msgstr "Cråssès letes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The state of this checkbox decides if the context should be rendered using a "
"boldface font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "Italic"
msgstr "Clintcheyès letes"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The state of this checkbox decides if the context should be rendered using "
"italic font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Normal"
msgstr "Normå"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button displays the color for drawing the style in normal mode, when "
"the text is not selected that is. To change the color, click the button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selected"
msgstr "Tchoezi"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button displays the color for drawing the style when the text is "
"selected. To change the color, click the button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: configuring.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Default"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This checkbox, only available in the <guibutton>Highlight Modes</guibutton> "
"tab shows if the style is using its default values. It will automatically "
"become unchecked if you change any properties of the style. Check it to "
"reset a style to using defaults."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Default Styles Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "To change any of the default styles, set its properties as desired."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Highlight Modes Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid "syntax highlighting, configuring"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can change the most important properties of each available "
"highlight mode. First, use the <guibutton>Highlight</guibutton> dropdown to "
"choose a mode to work on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Highlight modes are initially chosen based on the &MIME; type and extension "
"of the file. To change the list for the current selection, edit the "
"<guibutton>File Extensions</guibutton> and <guibutton>Mime Types</guibutton>"
" entries. Alternatively, press the wizard button to the right of the "
"<guibutton>Mime Types</guibutton> entry. This will show a dialog displaying "
"all available &MIME; types to choose from. Using it will edit the &MIME; "
"types as well as the file extensions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &MIME; type chooser dialog displays a tree of available &MIME; types, "
"with a description and the patterns for the &MIME; type. To include a &MIME; "
"type, check the box beside it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can change the style properties of any context as described above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:644
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the tab, below the highlight properties, you see a button "
"labeled <guibutton>Download</guibutton>"
". Pressing it will attempt to connect to the &kate; website and fetch a list "
"of available syntax highlight modes which you can update or add."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Plugins Group"
msgstr "Li groupe des tchôke-divins"

#. Tag: primary
#: configuring.docbook:659
#, no-c-format
msgid "plugins, configuring"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:659
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group contains pages related to plugins. Apart from the Manager "
"configuration page, some plugins provide individual configuration options. "
"For information on these, see the documentation for the individual plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuring.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Plugin Manager Page"
msgstr "Li pådje di manaedjmitn des tchôke-divins"

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page provides the means of loading/unloading plugins, and minimal "
"information about individual plugins."
msgstr ""
"Cisse pådje ci c' est po tcherdjî/distcherdjî les tchôke-divins, eyet "
"po des informåcions di båze so tchaeke des tchôke-divins."

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To load an unloaded plugin, select it in the <guibutton>Available "
"Plugins</guibutton> pane and use the arrow buttons to move it to the "
"<guibutton>Loaded Plugins</guibutton> pane."
msgstr ""
"Po tcherdjî on tchôke-divins ki n' l' est nén co, tchoezixhoz l' e "
"panea des <guibutton>Tchôke-divins k' i gn a</guibutton>"
" eyet eployîz les botons avou les fletches pol displaecî viè l' panea "
"<guibutton>Tchôke-divins tcherdjîs</guibutton>."

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To unload a loaded plugin, select it in the <guibutton>Loaded "
"Plugins</guibutton> pane and use the arrow buttons to move it to the "
"<guibutton>Available buttons</guibutton> pane."
msgstr ""
"Po distcherdjî on tchôke-divins di tcherdjî, tchoezixhoz l' e panea "
"<guibutton>Tchôke-divins tcherdjîs</guibutton> eyet eployîz les botons "
"avou les fletches pol displaecî viè l' panea des <guibutton>Botons k' i "
"gn a</guibutton>."

#. Tag: para
#: configuring.docbook:679
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To view a minimal description and information about a plugin, select it and "
"the information will be available below the lists."
msgstr ""
"Po vey on court discrijhaedje eyet informåcion so on tchôke-divins, "
"tchoezixhoz l' eyet si informåcion serè håynêye pa dzo les djivêyes."
